    "This is a topology sensitivity test on already inspected development systems, not an external confirmation.",
    "SPARC uses an axisymmetric midplane tidal closure; BCG, CLASH, raw clusters, and the Solar System use a spherical density closure.",
    "Under spherical closure the middle-to-maximum tidal ratio is a re-expression of local-to-mean density; this stage does not supply a common tensor map.",
    "The lower and upper pivots bracket the measured development distributions: SPARC is mostly low, CLASH mostly high, and BCGs largely intermediate.",
    "The two-tail and middle-band gates are exact complements, so their comparison isolates placement rather than a change in gate normalization.",
    "The RG ceiling 2.75 and n=1.5 Solar screen are unchanged from the preceding tidal stages.",
